# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Packaging (src layout)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Logs
logs/

# Run-chain scratch summaries. scripts/run_*.sh write these -- they are
# regenerable output of summarize_runs.py, not source, and RESULTS.md is the
# place a reading gets written down.
*_STATUS.md

# LaTeX build artifacts
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.toc
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.pdf
# The compiled figure-review document; the fig*.pdf beside it are source.
paper/figures/figures.pdf

# Results: what is committed and what is not.
#
# COMMITTED -- the reproducible evidentiary base:
#   results/data/*.csv        the tidy per-run summaries (runs.csv, runs_v2.csv)
#   results/data/runs/*.json  the per-run result rows those CSVs are BUILT from.
#                             ~6 MB. collect_runs.py regenerates the CSV from
#                             these; nothing regenerates these but re-running the
#                             work, so committing them is what makes the CSV a
#                             reproducible artifact rather than an unbacked one.
#   results/runs/*/*.json     per-round histories + the run's spec. ~550 MB raw
#                             and ~34% of that packed, which is what lets any
#                             training curve be re-plotted from the repo alone.
#
# NOT COMMITTED -- large and effectively incompressible:
#   *.pt under any checkpoints/ dir. ~34 GB of model checkpoints and per-client
#   weights; a sample gzips to 92% of its size, so git buys nothing and the tree
#   becomes unclonable. Shared out of band instead.
#   Per-run stdout logs. ~12 GB, and 9 of them exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit
#   outright -- they are Flower/Ray retry tracebacks, not evidence.
# results/baselines/ is the Config DEFAULT output_dir, so the test suite and any
# ad-hoc run land there. Only its 17 committed v1 figures belong in git; the
# histories that appear beside them are transient. (Before this file listed
# committed paths explicitly, a blanket results/**/*.json hid them.)
results/baselines/**/*.json

results/**/checkpoints/
results/checkpoints/
# ...with ONE tracked exception, 740 files / 629 MB under
# results/experiments/exp7_mechanistic/*/checkpoints/. Those predate this rule
# and are not orphans: analysis/mechanistic.py::run_analysis and
# scripts/plotting/plot_exp7_mechanistic.py read them directly, so untracking
# them would leave both unable to run from a fresh clone.
*.pt
results/data/runs/*.log
results/**/*.log

# Tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
